§ `Covid-19 (Gathering Control) (Jersey) Order 2020 - as last in force (repealed)`
-- Source: R&O.166/2020 as amended (R&O.189/2020, R&O.1/2021, R&O.5/2021, R&O.11/2021, L.6/2021)
-- Official page: https://www.jerseylaw.je/laws/current/ro_166_2020
-- Status: repealed. Parallel skeleton with GCO-first-version.l4 to make diffs easy to spot.
-- DIFFS vs first enacted are called out with -- DIFF: markers.

§§ `1 Interpretation - domain model`

DECLARE CeremonyOfficersRole IS ONE OF
    `persons constituting the marriage`
    `persons constituting the civil partnership`
    `persons constituting the funeral officers`
    `not a wedding civil partnership or funeral`

DECLARE Gathering HAS
    `number of persons taking part`                                IS A NUMBER
    -- TWO INDEPENDENT PREDICATES, NOT A PARTITION. A gathering can be both:
    -- vows on the lawn followed by a reception in the restaurant is one
    -- gathering that took place outdoors and indoors. These two were once
    -- written as a complement -- `takes place outdoors MEANS NOT takes place
    -- indoors` -- which made them mutually exclusive and let exactly one of
    -- Article 3's two caps fire, because both read the same head count. A
    -- 15-person mixed gathering then breached the 10-person indoor cap or
    -- cleared the 20-person outdoor one purely according to which box the
    -- responsible person ticked. The Order's own drafting contemplates mixed
    -- venues: PubliclyAccessiblePremisesGathering below counts the persons
    -- gathering in the indoor AREAS of a premises -- plural, of one premises.
    --
    -- SEAM, LEFT OPEN. One `number of persons taking part` still cannot apply
    -- two caps to two phases of one gathering. Closing it needs per-area counts
    -- AND the words of R&O.166/2020 Art.3, which this workspace does not hold,
    -- to say whether each cap governs its own phase or the gathering entire.
    `takes place indoors`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `takes place outdoors`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a school group of pupils and staff at school premises`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a wedding, civil partnership ceremony or funeral`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `ceremony officers role`                                       IS A CeremonyOfficersRole
    `number of ceremony officers`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `number of guests`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `total of officers and guests`                                 IS A NUMBER
        MEANS `number of ceremony officers` PLUS `number of guests`
    `is for the purposes of work`                                  IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE PubliclyAccessiblePremisesGathering HAS
    `number of persons gathering in the indoor areas`              IS A NUMBER
    `premises are publicly accessible`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is responsible for the premises`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person allowed the gathering`                             IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Participant HAS
    `name`                                                         IS A STRING
    `is a critical worker as defined in guidance published by the Minister for Health and Social Services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fails to take part by reason of force majeure as a critical worker` IS A BOOLEAN
        MEANS `is a critical worker as defined in guidance published by the Minister for Health and Social Services`

DECLARE ResponsiblePerson HAS
    `name`                                                         IS A STRING
    `is an official from Visit Jersey escorting a pre-arranged automotive tour of the island for news and travel journalists who are guests of the Jersey Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fails to prevent the gathering by reason of force majeure as a holiday industrial tour guide` IS A BOOLEAN
        MEANS `is an official from Visit Jersey escorting a pre-arranged automotive tour of the island for news and travel journalists who are guests of the Jersey Government`

DECLARE Article3Situation HAS
    gathering                                                      IS A Gathering
    participant                                                    IS A Participant

DECLARE Article7Situation HAS
    gathering                                                      IS A PubliclyAccessiblePremisesGathering
    responsible                                                    IS A ResponsiblePerson

§§ `3 Restriction on gatherings - as last in force`
-- DIFF: first enacted flat 10-person cap at any premises.
-- Last in force splits venue kind (amended by R&O.189/2020 and L.6/2021):
--   Art.3(1) outdoor gathering of more than 20 people
--   Art.3(2) indoor gathering of more than 10 people

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 3 outdoor size limit is exceeded` g IF
        g's `takes place outdoors`
    AND g's `number of persons taking part` GREATER THAN 20

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 3 indoor size limit is exceeded` g IF
        g's `takes place indoors`
    AND g's `number of persons taking part` GREATER THAN 10

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 3 size limit is exceeded` g IF
        `Article 3 outdoor size limit is exceeded` g
    OR  `Article 3 indoor size limit is exceeded` g

§§ `4 Exception - school group of pupils`
-- Unchanged from first enacted.

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 4 school-group exception applies` g IF
    g's `is a school group of pupils and staff at school premises`

§§ `5 Exception - wedding, civil partnership or funeral`
-- DIFF: first enacted single "must not exceed 20" total.
-- Last in force (post R&O.11/2021 etc.):
--   Art.5(1)  may gather in numbers that would otherwise breach Art.3(1) or (2)
--   Art.5(1A) outdoor: officers + guests must not exceed 20 people in total
--   Art.5(1B) indoor:  officers + guests must not exceed 20 people in total
-- Both (1A) and (1B) end at the same numeric roof in the final consolidated text;
-- they are kept separate so a later re-tightening of either limb is easy to re-encode.

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 5 wedding funeral exception is available` g IF
    g's `is a wedding, civil partnership ceremony or funeral`

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 5 outdoor size cap is respected` g IF
        g's `takes place outdoors`
    AND g's `total of officers and guests` AT MOST 20

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 5 indoor size cap is respected` g IF
        g's `takes place indoors`
    AND g's `total of officers and guests` AT MOST 20

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 5 size cap is respected` g IF
        `Article 5 outdoor size cap is respected` g
    OR  `Article 5 indoor size cap is respected` g

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 5 wedding funeral exception applies` g IF
        `Article 5 wedding funeral exception is available` g
    AND `Article 5 size cap is respected` g

§§ `6 Exception - work`
-- Unchanged from first enacted.

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 6 work exception applies` g IF
    g's `is for the purposes of work`

§§ `3 read with 4, 5 and 6 - restricted gathering`

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Article 3 exception applies` g IF
        `Article 4 school-group exception applies` g
    OR  `Article 5 wedding funeral exception applies` g
    OR  `Article 6 work exception applies` g

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gathering is a restricted gathering under Article 3` g IF
        `Article 3 size limit is exceeded` g
    AND NOT `an Article 3 exception applies` g

GIVEN g IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person must not take part in the gathering under Article 3` g IF
    `the gathering is a restricted gathering under Article 3` g

§§ `7 Restriction on gatherings in publicly accessible premises`
-- Unchanged in substance from first enacted: indoor more than 10.

GIVEN p IS A PubliclyAccessiblePremisesGathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 7 size limit is exceeded` p IF
    p's `number of persons gathering in the indoor areas` GREATER THAN 10

GIVEN p IS A PubliclyAccessiblePremisesGathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the responsible person must not allow the gathering under Article 7` p IF
        p's `premises are publicly accessible`
    AND p's `the person is responsible for the premises`
    AND `Article 7 size limit is exceeded` p

§§ `9 Offences and penalties`

@export Whether the participant commits an Article 3 offence (taking part in a restricted gathering, subject to the critical-worker force-majeure defence)
GIVEN s IS A Article3Situation @desc Situation under Art.3: the gathering facts plus the participant's critical-worker status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an Article 3 offence` IF
        `the gathering is a restricted gathering under Article 3` (s's gathering)
    AND NOT s's participant's `fails to take part by reason of force majeure as a critical worker`

@export Whether the responsible person commits an Article 7 offence (allowing an oversize indoor gathering on publicly accessible premises, subject to the Visit Jersey tour-guide force-majeure defence)
GIVEN s IS A Article7Situation @desc Situation under Art.7: the premises gathering facts plus the responsible person's tour-guide status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an Article 7 offence` IF
        `the responsible person must not allow the gathering under Article 7` (s's gathering)
    AND s's gathering's `the person allowed the gathering`
    AND NOT s's responsible's `fails to prevent the gathering by reason of force majeure as a holiday industrial tour guide`

@export The maximum fine in pounds for an Article 3 or Article 7 offence under this Order (level 2 on the standard scale: 1000)
GIVEN has_committed_offence IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the person has committed an Art.3 or Art.7 offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Article 9 maximum fine in pounds` IS
    IF has_committed_offence THEN 1000 ELSE 0

@export Whether a person must not take part in the gathering under Article 3 (size limit exceeded and no school / wedding or funeral / work exception)
GIVEN g IS A Gathering @desc The gathering: size, indoor or outdoor, and which if any of the Art.4-6 exception predicates hold
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person must not take part under Article 3` IF
    `a person must not take part in the gathering under Article 3` g

@export Whether the responsible person must not allow the gathering under Article 7
GIVEN p IS A PubliclyAccessiblePremisesGathering @desc Publicly accessible premises facts: indoor headcount, responsibility, and whether allowed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a responsible person must not allow under Article 7` IF
    `the responsible person must not allow the gathering under Article 7` p

§§ `test cases - as last in force`

`ordinary indoor of 11` MEANS Gathering WITH
    `number of persons taking part`                            IS 11
    `takes place indoors`                                      IS TRUE
    `takes place outdoors`                                     IS FALSE
    `is a school group of pupils and staff at school premises` IS FALSE
    `is a wedding, civil partnership ceremony or funeral`      IS FALSE
    `ceremony officers role`                                   IS `not a wedding civil partnership or funeral`
    `number of ceremony officers`                              IS 0
    `number of guests`                                         IS 0
    `is for the purposes of work`                              IS FALSE

-- DIFF: outdoor of 11 was prohibited under first enacted (flat 10); lawful under last in force (outdoor rooftop 20)
`ordinary outdoor of 11` MEANS Gathering WITH
    `number of persons taking part`                            IS 11
    `takes place indoors`                                      IS FALSE
    `takes place outdoors`                                     IS TRUE
    `is a school group of pupils and staff at school premises` IS FALSE
    `is a wedding, civil partnership ceremony or funeral`      IS FALSE
    `ceremony officers role`                                   IS `not a wedding civil partnership or funeral`
    `number of ceremony officers`                              IS 0
    `number of guests`                                         IS 0
    `is for the purposes of work`                              IS FALSE

`ordinary outdoor of 21` MEANS Gathering WITH
    `number of persons taking part`                            IS 21
    `takes place indoors`                                      IS FALSE
    `takes place outdoors`                                     IS TRUE
    `is a school group of pupils and staff at school premises` IS FALSE
    `is a wedding, civil partnership ceremony or funeral`      IS FALSE
    `ceremony officers role`                                   IS `not a wedding civil partnership or funeral`
    `number of ceremony officers`                              IS 0
    `number of guests`                                         IS 0
    `is for the purposes of work`                              IS FALSE

`school of 30` MEANS Gathering WITH
    `number of persons taking part`                            IS 30
    `takes place indoors`                                      IS TRUE
    `takes place outdoors`                                     IS FALSE
    `is a school group of pupils and staff at school premises` IS TRUE
    `is a wedding, civil partnership ceremony or funeral`      IS FALSE
    `ceremony officers role`                                   IS `not a wedding civil partnership or funeral`
    `number of ceremony officers`                              IS 0
    `number of guests`                                         IS 0
    `is for the purposes of work`                              IS FALSE

`wedding of 2 officers and 18 guests` MEANS Gathering WITH
    `number of persons taking part`                            IS 20
    `takes place indoors`                                      IS TRUE
    `takes place outdoors`                                     IS FALSE
    `is a school group of pupils and staff at school premises` IS FALSE
    `is a wedding, civil partnership ceremony or funeral`      IS TRUE
    `ceremony officers role`                                   IS `persons constituting the marriage`
    `number of ceremony officers`                              IS 2
    `number of guests`                                         IS 18
    `is for the purposes of work`                              IS FALSE

`wedding of 2 officers and 19 guests over cap` MEANS Gathering WITH
    `number of persons taking part`                            IS 21
    `takes place indoors`                                      IS TRUE
    `takes place outdoors`                                     IS FALSE
    `is a school group of pupils and staff at school premises` IS FALSE
    `is a wedding, civil partnership ceremony or funeral`      IS TRUE
    `ceremony officers role`                                   IS `persons constituting the marriage`
    `number of ceremony officers`                              IS 2
    `number of guests`                                         IS 19
    `is for the purposes of work`                              IS FALSE

`outdoor wedding of 2 officers and 18 guests` MEANS Gathering WITH
    `number of persons taking part`                            IS 20
    `takes place indoors`                                      IS FALSE
    `takes place outdoors`                                     IS TRUE
    `is a school group of pupils and staff at school premises` IS FALSE
    `is a wedding, civil partnership ceremony or funeral`      IS TRUE
    `ceremony officers role`                                   IS `persons constituting the marriage`
    `number of ceremony officers`                              IS 2
    `number of guests`                                         IS 18
    `is for the purposes of work`                              IS FALSE

-- THE CASE THE OLD MODEL COULD NOT STATE. Vows on the lawn, reception in the
-- restaurant: one gathering, both venues. Under the complement this record was
-- unwritable -- `takes place outdoors` was whatever `takes place indoors` was
-- not -- so the responsible person's answer to a single question decided which
-- of Article 3's two caps applied to a 15-person party, and the other cap was
-- never tested. Fifteen clears the outdoor 20 and breaches the indoor 10, so
-- ticking "outdoor" bought five extra heads. Now both caps see the gathering
-- and the stricter one governs, which is the conservative reading; whether the
-- Order in fact means each cap to govern only its own phase is the seam left
-- open at the field declaration, and is not settled here.
`mixed-venue party of 15` MEANS Gathering WITH
    `number of persons taking part`                            IS 15
    `takes place indoors`                                      IS TRUE
    `takes place outdoors`                                     IS TRUE
    `is a school group of pupils and staff at school premises` IS FALSE
    `is a wedding, civil partnership ceremony or funeral`      IS FALSE
    `ceremony officers role`                                   IS `not a wedding civil partnership or funeral`
    `number of ceremony officers`                              IS 0
    `number of guests`                                         IS 0
    `is for the purposes of work`                              IS FALSE

`worksite of 25` MEANS Gathering WITH
    `number of persons taking part`                            IS 25
    `takes place indoors`                                      IS TRUE
    `takes place outdoors`                                     IS FALSE
    `is a school group of pupils and staff at school premises` IS FALSE
    `is a wedding, civil partnership ceremony or funeral`      IS FALSE
    `ceremony officers role`                                   IS `not a wedding civil partnership or funeral`
    `number of ceremony officers`                              IS 0
    `number of guests`                                         IS 0
    `is for the purposes of work`                              IS TRUE

`pub indoor of 12` MEANS PubliclyAccessiblePremisesGathering WITH
    `number of persons gathering in the indoor areas` IS 12
    `premises are publicly accessible`               IS TRUE
    `the person is responsible for the premises`     IS TRUE
    `the person allowed the gathering`               IS TRUE

`pub indoor of 10` MEANS PubliclyAccessiblePremisesGathering WITH
    `number of persons gathering in the indoor areas` IS 10
    `premises are publicly accessible`               IS TRUE
    `the person is responsible for the premises`     IS TRUE
    `the person allowed the gathering`               IS TRUE

`ordinary participant` MEANS Participant WITH
    `name` IS "Pat"
    `is a critical worker as defined in guidance published by the Minister for Health and Social Services` IS FALSE

`critical worker participant` MEANS Participant WITH
    `name` IS "Chris"
    `is a critical worker as defined in guidance published by the Minister for Health and Social Services` IS TRUE

`ordinary landlord` MEANS ResponsiblePerson WITH
    `name` IS "Les"
    `is an official from Visit Jersey escorting a pre-arranged automotive tour of the island for news and travel journalists who are guests of the Jersey Government` IS FALSE

`visit jersey official` MEANS ResponsiblePerson WITH
    `name` IS "Vic"
    `is an official from Visit Jersey escorting a pre-arranged automotive tour of the island for news and travel journalists who are guests of the Jersey Government` IS TRUE

`Pat at ordinary indoor of 11` MEANS Article3Situation WITH
    gathering   IS `ordinary indoor of 11`
    participant IS `ordinary participant`

`Chris critical worker at ordinary indoor of 11` MEANS Article3Situation WITH
    gathering   IS `ordinary indoor of 11`
    participant IS `critical worker participant`

`Pat at ordinary outdoor of 21` MEANS Article3Situation WITH
    gathering   IS `ordinary outdoor of 21`
    participant IS `ordinary participant`

`Les allows pub indoor of 12` MEANS Article7Situation WITH
    gathering   IS `pub indoor of 12`
    responsible IS `ordinary landlord`

`Vic tour guide allows pub indoor of 12` MEANS Article7Situation WITH
    gathering   IS `pub indoor of 12`
    responsible IS `visit jersey official`

#ASSERT `a person must not take part under Article 3` `ordinary indoor of 11`
#ASSERT NOT (`a person must not take part under Article 3` `ordinary outdoor of 11`)
#ASSERT `a person must not take part under Article 3` `ordinary outdoor of 21`
#ASSERT NOT (`a person must not take part under Article 3` `school of 30`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a person must not take part under Article 3` `wedding of 2 officers and 18 guests`)
#ASSERT `a person must not take part under Article 3` `wedding of 2 officers and 19 guests over cap`
#ASSERT NOT (`a person must not take part under Article 3` `outdoor wedding of 2 officers and 18 guests`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a person must not take part under Article 3` `worksite of 25`)

-- The mixed venue, pinned at both caps. The indoor limb fires because 15 > 10;
-- the outdoor limb does not, because 15 is inside 20. Both are now evaluated,
-- where the complement let only one of them be reachable per gathering.
#ASSERT     `Article 3 indoor size limit is exceeded`  `mixed-venue party of 15`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 3 outdoor size limit is exceeded` `mixed-venue party of 15`)
#ASSERT     `a person must not take part under Article 3` `mixed-venue party of 15`

#ASSERT `a responsible person must not allow under Article 7` `pub indoor of 12`
#ASSERT NOT (`a responsible person must not allow under Article 7` `pub indoor of 10`)

#ASSERT `the person commits an Article 3 offence` `Pat at ordinary indoor of 11`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person commits an Article 3 offence` `Chris critical worker at ordinary indoor of 11`)
#ASSERT `the person commits an Article 3 offence` `Pat at ordinary outdoor of 21`
#ASSERT `the person commits an Article 7 offence` `Les allows pub indoor of 12`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person commits an Article 7 offence` `Vic tour guide allows pub indoor of 12`)

#ASSERT `Article 9 maximum fine in pounds` TRUE EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `Article 9 maximum fine in pounds` FALSE EQUALS 0
